# strand-eval reference recordings (docs/eval.md, "Reference recordings"). Written by `strand-eval approve` and `verdict`; a block edited by hand fails its seal.
ref "popup-shrink-centred"
verdict good
note "growth: read against the reference: the popup springs its height 52 -> 91.3 -> 90 taller (k60-75) and its width 164 -> 222.7 -> 220 wider (k107-123) from its anchor where the reference snapped; the card's own overshoot past the buffer is followed and cut by it, #mark is still in every settled segment; and (review) while the box is drawn short of its buffer the surface takes input in that box alone, the margin passing the pointer, and its whole buffer again at rest: popup#pop k34-115 (45 frames, first i=2,0,216,50)"
